1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,586
Welcome to Azul!

2
00:00:01,906 --> 00:00:04,871
This first short video shows what the game is about.

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,481
Azul is a game for two to four players.

4
00:00:08,801 --> 00:00:11,788
In these videos, two friends play: Ana and Ben.

5
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:14,115
They take turns.

6
00:00:14,435 --> 00:00:15,865
First, Ana plays.

7
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:18,161
Then Ben plays.

8
00:00:18,481 --> 00:00:20,337
Then Ana again, and so on.

9
00:00:20,657 --> 00:00:22,235
Each go is called a turn.

10
00:00:23,366 --> 00:00:25,542
The game uses small square pieces.

11
00:00:25,862 --> 00:00:27,163
They are called tiles.

12
00:00:27,483 --> 00:00:31,153
There are five colours: blue, yellow, red, black and white.

13
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:34,997
Each colour also has its own mark and letter.

14
00:00:35,317 --> 00:00:37,088
So you never need colour alone.

15
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,482
Each player has their own player board.

16
00:00:40,802 --> 00:00:42,850
Look at Ana's board, on the left.

17
00:00:43,966 --> 00:00:45,972
The grid on the right is her wall.

18
00:00:46,292 --> 00:00:48,532
Her goal is to decorate it with tiles.

19
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:52,726
In the middle of the table, tiles wait on small discs.

20
00:00:53,046 --> 00:00:55,009
The next video gives them a name.

21
00:00:57,349 --> 00:00:59,653
On her turn, Ana takes some tiles.

22
00:00:59,973 --> 00:01:02,021
They wait on the left side of her board.

23
00:01:04,349 --> 00:01:06,739
Later, one tile moves onto her wall.

24
00:01:07,059 --> 00:01:08,915
Tiles on the wall score points.

25
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,920
This one scores one point.

26
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:14,444
Her points are shown at the top of her board.

27
00:01:15,566 --> 00:01:18,638
Players collect tiles, then move them to their walls.

28
00:01:18,958 --> 00:01:20,686
That cycle is called a round.

29
00:01:21,006 --> 00:01:22,649
A game has several rounds.

30
00:01:23,766 --> 00:01:26,902
When the game ends, the player with the most points wins.

31
00:01:27,222 --> 00:01:28,758
That player is the winner.

32
00:01:29,866 --> 00:01:30,762
Remember.

33
00:01:31,082 --> 00:01:33,258
Players take turns collecting tiles.

34
00:01:33,578 --> 00:01:35,434
Tiles on your wall score points.

35
00:01:35,754 --> 00:01:37,738
And the most points at the end wins.

36
00:01:38,058 --> 00:01:40,085
Next up: getting the game ready.
